# --- 11-12 (w10): Mrs. Elaine Hollins - the islander of The Lullaby Frequency (optional, no quest step). The owner's
# widow sits on the yard's concrete by the barrels, facing the slipway the player comes up; she hears the song through
# the floor. Her first answer opens the cellar hatch in the sea cave under Smokehouse Hill (journal page), her second
# names the night shift (journal page), her third is a goodbye.
# (r4: on a chair - a sitter needs a seat: on the bare ground the sit pose floats, as at Shelter Atoll)
place Placeable_Chair_Wood hcelainechair at -15 -9 ground sit yaw=90
prop hcelainechair obj.name=hcelainechair
place Story_Islander hcelaine at -15 -9 ground yaw=90
prop hcelaine obj.name=Mrs. Elaine Hollins
prop hcelaine islander.character=Elaine
prop hcelaine islander.pose=sit
prop hcelaine talk.text=You hear it too? The lullaby. It comes up through the floor.\n> Where does it come from?\n> Who else heard it?\n> I hear nothing.
prop hcelaine on.choice1=journal|Mrs. Elaine Hollins: the cellar|Elaine says the song is loudest in the sea cave under Smokehouse Hill, the hill with the radio mast. Her husband kept the cannery's cellar in there, under a steel hatch. The cave's mouth is on the shore at the foot of the hill, by the water. She has unlocked the hatch for you.\nmessage||Under the hill. My husband's cellar is in the sea cave at the foot of Smokehouse Hill, by the water - I have unlocked the hatch. Go and listen.
prop hcelaine on.choice2=journal|Mrs. Elaine Hollins: who heard it|Ada Brann heard it first, on the radio at the mast. Then Jonna Hale at the gutting table, Tobias Grell in the ice cave and Rolf Iversen up in his spotter plane. The whole night shift heard it and walked down to the water. Only the boy Pim stayed - he hums it now.\nmessage||Ada first, on the radio. Then Jonna, Tobias, Rolf. They all walked down to the water. Only Pim stayed.
prop hcelaine on.choice3=message||No? Then sit with me a while. At twelve past three you will.

